WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:18.242
Peter slid up his tunnel and went out to make arrangements for Wendy, John, and Michael's trip home.

2
00:00:18.243 --> 00:00:23.163
He gave orders to the Indians to guide Wendy and her brothers through the woods.

3
00:00:23.164 --> 00:00:28.731
Then Peter returned to the underground home, where an unfortunate sight greeted him.

4
00:00:28.732 --> 00:00:33.383
Upset that they were going to lose Wendy, the Lost Boys were frantic.

5
00:00:33.384 --> 00:00:39.010
"After you leave, things will be worse than before you came!"

6
00:00:39.011 --> 00:00:41.268
"We won't let you go."

7
00:00:41.269 --> 00:00:43.875
"We'll keep you as our prisoner."

8
00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:45.538
"Chain her up!"

9
00:00:45.539 --> 00:00:47.319
They shouted at her.

10
00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:53.217
Only Tootles protected Wendy. He took out his sword and faced the other boys.

11
00:00:53.218 --> 00:00:56.490
This wasn't like the usual Tootles.

12
00:00:56.491 --> 00:01:00.573
He stood up tall and straight and proud.

13
00:01:00.574 --> 00:01:07.572
"I will strike the first one who does not behave well toward Wendy," he said bravely.

14
00:01:07.573 --> 00:01:10.026
The other boys backed off.

15
00:01:10.027 --> 00:01:15.810
Then they noticed Peter. They saw that he would not support them either.

16
00:01:15.811 --> 00:01:22.208
"I would never," said Peter, "keep a girl in Neverland against her will.

17
00:01:22.209 --> 00:01:27.717
I've asked the Indians to guide you through the woods," he explained to Wendy.

18
00:01:27.718 --> 00:01:33.888
"Then Tinker Bell will take you across the sea. Wake Tinker Bell up, Nibs."

19
00:01:33.889 --> 00:01:38.254
Nibs knocked twice on the wall beside Tinker Bell's nook.

20
00:01:38.255 --> 00:01:43.265
Her curtains were drawn, but of course she had been listening all along.

21
00:01:43.266 --> 00:01:49.385
The fairy was delighted that Wendy was leaving, but she did not want to be her guide.

22
00:01:49.386 --> 00:01:53.654
Without opening her curtains, she refused.

23
00:01:53.655 --> 00:01:57.951
"Tink says she won't go!" Nibs yelled.

24
00:01:57.952 --> 00:02:01.646
He was surprised that she dared to disobey Peter.

25
00:02:01.647 --> 00:02:04.858
Peter went directly to Tinker Bell himself.

26
00:02:04.859 --> 00:02:11.589
"Tink," he demanded, "if you don't get up and dress at once, I will open your curtains.

27
00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:15.153
Then we will see you in your nightgown."

28
00:02:15.154 --> 00:02:18.852
This made the vain fairy leap to the floor.

29
00:02:18.853 --> 00:02:22.486
"Who said I wasn't getting up?" she cried.

30
00:02:22.487 --> 00:02:28.067
Meanwhile, Wendy, John, and Michael were getting ready for their journey.

31
00:02:28.068 --> 00:02:34.145
The Lost Boys watched, growing sadder and sadder at the thought of Wendy leaving.

32
00:02:34.146 --> 00:02:44.978
When they began to cry, Wendy softly said, "Dear boys, if you want to come with me, I'm sure my mother and father will adopt you."

33
00:02:44.979 --> 00:02:52.096
This invitation was actually meant for Peter, but she offered it to the rest of the boys out of kindness.

34
00:02:52.097 --> 00:02:56.903
"Peter, can we go with Wendy?" they asked.

35
00:02:56.904 --> 00:03:00.722
"All right," he said with a bitter smile.

36
00:03:00.723 --> 00:03:03.611
They went to pack their knapsacks for the trip.

37
00:03:03.612 --> 00:03:07.942
Wendy and the boys both thought Peter would be joining them.

38
00:03:07.943 --> 00:03:12.630
But Peter, of course, had no intention of going.

39
00:03:12.631 --> 00:03:16.052
"Get your things, Peter," said Wendy.

40
00:03:16.053 --> 00:03:22.042
"No," he answered, pretending not to care. "I'm not going with you."

41
00:03:22.043 --> 00:03:29.747
Then to show that none of this mattered to him, he skipped around the room playing his flute.

42
00:03:29.748 --> 00:03:33.781
"Don't you want to find your mother?" Wendy asked.

43
00:03:33.782 --> 00:03:36.237
She didn't want to leave him behind.

44
00:03:36.238 --> 00:03:41.424
"Even if I had one, I hardly remember her," said Peter.

45
00:03:41.425 --> 00:03:44.481
"Anyway, she would just force me to grow up.

46
00:03:44.482 --> 00:03:48.580
And I want to stay a little boy and have fun."

47
00:03:48.581 --> 00:03:55.340
When Wendy told the boys that Peter wasn't coming, they wondered if he would let them go without him.

48
00:03:55.341 --> 00:04:00.948
"Let's not make a fuss," said Peter, too proud to show his feelings.

49
00:04:00.949 --> 00:04:05.926
"Good-bye, boys. Good-bye, Wendy." He held out his hand to her.

50
00:04:05.927 --> 00:04:11.120
She took it sadly, but wished he had hugged or kissed her instead.

51
00:04:11.121 --> 00:04:17.088
"Please remember to eat properly, Peter," she said, almost crying.

52
00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:22.206
"And don't forget to take your medicine. I've put it in a cup for you."

53
00:04:22.207 --> 00:04:29.079
A sad moment followed. The sadness made Peter uncomfortable, so he interrupted the silence.

54
00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:34.447
"Are you ready, Tink?" he called out. "Lead the way."

55
00:04:34.448 --> 00:04:38.341
Tinker Bell darted up the nearest tunnel to the outside world.

56
00:04:38.342 --> 00:04:44.656
But before anyone could follow her, the sound of a brutal battle erupted above.

57
00:04:44.657 --> 00:04:53.726
At that very moment, the pirates had attacked the Indians on top of the Lost Boys' home.
